'''Lloguer i Viatges de l'Istme, S.A.''' (LVI), trading as '''IstmeLloguer''', is a Balboan car rental and coach tour operator based in [[Sant Cristòfor]]. The company operates a nationwide car rental network under the IstmeLloguer brand and a fleet of coach buses serving the tourism and corporate transport markets. It is listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] under the ticker LVI and is a constituent of the [[SCX 100]] index.

== History ==

LVI was founded in 1989 by Miquel Cardona i Puig, a former manager at a Sant Cristòfor travel agency, who identified that the growing tourism sector — particularly visitors arriving through the [[Portnou|Port de Portnou]] and the city's airports — lacked adequate car rental infrastructure. The company began with a single rental desk at the Portnou ferry terminal and a fleet of 40 vehicles.

The company expanded rapidly in the 1990s as tourism grew, opening rental locations at airports, ports, and urban centres across the country. The reunification-era infrastructure boom and the establishment of the [[BTPMEU]] in 1998 increased both tourist arrivals and business travel, driving demand for rental vehicles. LVI was listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] in 2001.

In 2004, LVI acquired Coach Tours Balboa, a small coach operator based in [[Sant Bart]], establishing its tour bus division. The acquisition gave LVI a fleet of 18 coaches and access to the interior tourism market, including routes to the [[Yalabirga Mountain Range|Yalabirga highlands]] and the cooperative farm districts of [[Jala Province|Jala]].

The company invested in electric rental vehicles in the 2010s, initially purchasing [[SKQ]] entry-level EVs for its Sant Cristòfor fleet, where charging infrastructure was most developed. By 2026, approximately 35 per cent of the rental fleet was electric, concentrated in Estret Province.

== Operations ==

=== Car rental ===

LVI operates car rental locations at 12 sites across Balboa:

* [[Sant Cristòfor]] — three locations (airport, city centre, cruise terminal, [[Barcelona (Sant Cristòfor)|Barcelona]])
* [[Portnou]] — one location (city centre)
* [[Sant Bart]] — two locations (city centre, airport)
* [[Badia Curta]] — one location (airport)
* [[Novara]] — one location (city centre)
* [[Costabella]] — one location (city centre)
* [[Altaneu]] — one location (city centre)
* [[Sant Llàtzer]] — one location (city centre)
* [[Portblanc]] — one location (city centre)

The rental fleet comprises approximately 4,200 vehicles, ranging from economy cars to SUVs and vans. The fleet is sourced primarily from [[Distribució Automobilística de Balboa]] (DAB), the country's principal dealership group. Approximately 35 per cent of the fleet is electric, predominantly [[SKQ]], [[Vidal]], and [[Qhar]] models in Estret Province, with internal combustion engine vehicles from [[Sparc]], [[CdV]], and [[Yonezawa Motors|Yonezawa]] dominating the interior province fleets where charging infrastructure is limited. Qhar's solid-state battery technology, developed in Varkana, offers superior range and cold-weather performance, making it particularly suited to the highland rental routes around [[Sant Bart]] and [[Altaneu]].

Rental demand is driven by three segments: international tourists arriving through Sant Cristòfor and Portnou, domestic business travellers, and local residents requiring temporary vehicles for intercity travel or specific purposes. The interior locations — particularly Portblanc and Sant Llàtzer — serve primarily tourists visiting the canal region and the coastal resorts of [[Nurra Province|Nurra]].

=== Coach tours ===

LVI's coach division operates a fleet of 45 coaches from depots in [[Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Sant Bart]]. The division provides:

* Scheduled sightseeing tours of [[Sant Cristòfor]] and the [[Balboa Canal]]
* Multi-day interior tours covering the [[Yalabirga Mountain Range|Yalabirga highlands]], [[Jala Province|Jala]] agricultural districts, and the [[Nurra Province|Nurra]] coast
* Airport and port transfer services for tour groups and cruise passengers
* Corporate charter services for conventions and conferences in Sant Cristòfor

Coach bodies are supplied by [[Carrosseries de Balboa]], built on imported chassis. The coach fleet includes a growing number of electric coaches, primarily [[BYD Auto|BYD]] chassis fitted with Carrosseries de Balboa bodies, operating on urban sightseeing routes in Sant Cristòfor where the charging infrastructure supports daily operation.

